  = note: `print` renders its argument through `Display`. A nullable does not implement it until it is narrowed — `if x?: print(x)` — and an array, map or set never does (§3.4): print its `length()` or its elements, the same rule an f-string hole already enforces

error[SC0275]: `Array[Array[F64]]` cannot be printed: it does not implement `Display`
 --> tests/ui/types/print_of_a_collection.science:7:11
  |
7 |     print([[1.5], [2.5]])
